WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.638
Coding Exercise 3 brings together WHERE GROUP BY
HAVING and a calculated

00:00:04.662 --> 00:00:09.000
revenue measure The requirement says to use sales
rows where price is

00:00:09.025 --> 00:00:14.125
at least twenty-five That describes individual
source rows so write the condition

00:00:14.138 --> 00:00:17.688
in WHERE before the grouping step The grain is one
row per

00:00:17.712 --> 00:00:23.700
category so GROUP BY category You need
total_quantity which can be calculated

00:00:23.725 --> 00:00:28.512
with SUM quantity and total_revenue which can be
calculated by summing quantity

00:00:28.538 --> 00:00:34.150
times price Give both expressions clear aliases Next
keep

00:00:34.175 --> 00:00:39.250
only categories whose total quantity is greater than
ten That threshold depends

00:00:39.275 --> 00:00:43.775
on an aggregate so it belongs in HAVING Finally sort
the highest

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:48.288
revenue first Before clicking Run and Check inspect
the order of your

00:00:48.312 --> 00:00:53.750
clauses WHERE should come before GROUP BY HAVING
should come after GROUP

00:00:53.762 --> 00:00:58.012
BY If the query runs but the result seems wrong
verify the

00:00:58.038 --> 00:01:01.150
revenue expression and make sure the price filter is
applied to source

00:01:01.175 --> 00:01:05.662
rows rather than completed groups This exercise is a
strong test of

00:01:05.688 --> 00:01:08.575
whether you understand the logical stages of
aggregation
